# Model card: DPF pre-inspection concept route

*Rendered from run `{{ run_name }}` (profile `{{ profile }}`) on {{ today }}. Format after Mitchell et al. (2019).*

> **Trained and evaluated on synthetic data only.** Not validated on real filters; not for production use.

## Model details

- **Deployed model:** `{{ deployed }}`, gradient boosting (scikit-learn histogram boosting) over learned visual concepts, anomaly scores, flow features and metadata, with {{ models[deployed].calibration.method }} calibration.
- **Perception:** {{ cfg.perception.folds }} cross-fitted U-Nets (ResNet-18 encoder{{ ", ImageNet initialisation" if train.vision_models.unet[0].pretrained else ", random initialisation" }}) for {{ cfg.perception.classes | length }} defect classes.
- **Anomaly guard:** PatchCore-style memory bank of {{ train.vision_models.anomaly[0].bank_size }} patch features per fold from defect-free training faces.
- **Decision layer:** split-conformal outcome sets, cost-based thresholds, template rationale.
- **Version:** run `{{ run_name }}`, code `{{ commit }}`, data manifest `{{ manifest }}`, generator v{{ generator_version }}.
- **Licence:** MIT. Owner: Noyal George.

## Intended use

- Decision support at a pre-inspection station of a DPF cleaning line. The model recommends PROCEED, EXTENDED_CLEAN, QUARANTINE or REFER, with a rationale, before cleaning.
- A person confirms every QUARANTINE; the system never scraps a unit.
- **Out of scope:** real filters before validation on real data; new-build substrate inspection without retraining (see `docs/system_design.md`); any use as the sole basis for an emissions-compliance or safety decision.

## Factors

Lighting mode, camera profile, substrate material (cordierite, SiC), cell density, diameter, application and image quality. The robustness study and domain-shift study in `reports/validation_report.md` measure the effect of these.

## Metrics

Macro-F1, balanced accuracy, SCRAP recall and AUC, ΔP-ratio MAE, expected calibration error, conformal coverage. At the operating point: wrongful-scrap rate, scrap capture rate and REFER share.

## Evaluation data

The chronological test split ({{ d.n_test }} units), the novel-defect set (thermal melt, unseen in training) and the domain-shift set (new cell density and camera). Headline scores use the simulator's true outcome.

## Training data

The chronological training split after the validation gate. Labels are recorded downstream dispositions, about {{ stats.label_vs_truth_disagreement | pct }} of which differ from the true outcome because of test noise. See `docs/data_card.md`.

